---
---

<section id="how-it-works" class="section-spacing border-b border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--surface-tint)]">
  <div class="site-container">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-12">
      <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-[var(--brand)] mb-3">
        THE ORIGIN STORY
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-[var(--ink)] tracking-tight mb-4">
        Why I built MastiDB
      </h2>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed prose-measure">
        A concise three-beat story about moving from operating distributed analytical systems to understanding the exact mechanics of bytes on disk.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3-Beat Story Cards -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-10">
      
      <!-- Beat 1: Druid & Query Performance -->
      <div class="p-7 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] shadow-sm hover:border-[var(--brand)]/30 transition-all flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-[var(--lavender)] border border-[var(--line)] text-[var(--brand)] font-mono font-bold text-sm flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
            01
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink)] mb-3">
            Operating Druid at Scale
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
            Working on Apache Druid and query performance at Udaan and Percept Insight, I was fascinated by how analytical engines slice through millions of events in milliseconds. But managing clusters left me wanting to understand the engine under the hood.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-[var(--line)] text-xs font-mono text-[var(--brand)]">
          Distributed OLAP in practice
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Beat 2: Database Systems & Theory -->
      <div class="p-7 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] shadow-sm hover:border-[var(--brand)]/30 transition-all flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-[var(--dict-violet-bg)] border border-[var(--dict-violet-border)] text-[var(--dict-violet)] font-mono font-bold text-sm flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
            02
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink)] mb-3">
            Studying the Tradeoffs
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
            I immersed myself in database literature: columnar storage layouts, Roaring Bitmaps, dictionary encoding, and late materialization. Reading papers is one thing; discovering why a sorted dictionary eliminates string comparisons during sorting is another.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-[var(--line)] text-xs font-mono text-[var(--dict-violet)]">
          Columnar theory & papers
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Beat 3: Crafting MastiDB -->
      <div class="p-7 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] shadow-sm hover:border-[var(--brand)]/30 transition-all flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-[var(--result-green-bg)] border border-[var(--result-green-border)] text-[var(--result-green)] font-mono font-bold text-sm flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
            03
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink)] mb-3">
            Building from Scratch
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
            I wrote MastiDB from scratch to connect every idea directly: from raw bytes laid out in `.mastidb` files on disk, to memory-mapped slices, to hash partial merges. Writing it in Python (compiled with MyPyC) kept every design choice exposed and verifiable.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-[var(--line)] text-xs font-mono text-[var(--result-green)]">
          Disk bytes to query results
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Architectural Deep Dive Callout -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Looking for the full technical breakdown?</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">ARCHITECTURE.md details the folder layouts, byte offsets, and query execution pipelines.</p>
      </div>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/lokeshdevnani/mastidb/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded-xl bg-[var(--surface-tint)] border border-[var(--line)] hover:bg-[var(--lavender)] text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--brand)] hover:border-[var(--brand)]/30 transition-all whitespace-nowrap"
      >
        <span>Read ARCHITECTURE.md</span>
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
